{
  "issue": 9297,
  "status": "done",
  "branch": "claude/issue-9297-teaching-surfaces-scope-names",
  "pushed_sha": "20831dc1dc63965b7ea792e62b48780bc96ac478",
  "pr": "https://github.com/objectstack-ai/objectui/pull/9376",
  "premise_still_valid": true,
  "premise_notes": [
    "The card's ruling-dependent branch is genuinely collapsed: the objectui#9308 option-B ruling (5651694454, director confirmation 5651908975) removes the `data` root, so there is exactly one repair shape left. Verified against the tree, not against the card's paragraph.",
    "FALSIFICATION 1 - the card's lit control of 18 is not a count of ELEMENTS. Re-measured on my base 69aa9c017 with the card's own classifier: 18 tag-shaped hits across the five surfaces, reproducing the card exactly. Strip HTML comments first and it is 15 real JSX elements: three of the 18 are `SchemaRenderer` MENTIONS inside `doc-snippet: fragment` comments on expressions.md, which the word-boundary regex cannot tell from an element. Real elements 15 at base, 15 at head (none added, none deleted); tag-shaped hits fell 18 to 15 only because those three comments were rewritten.",
    "FALSIFICATION 2 - the card's bare-head-name classifier held `data` in the ACCEPTED root set, so it was structurally blind to the one site on these surfaces that the ruling actually breaks: content/docs/guide/architecture.md:55 authored `visible: \"${data.age > 18}\"`. The offender column under-counts by exactly the sites option B newly breaks. That site is repaired to `record.age` and the verdict flip is stated.",
    "FALSIFICATION 3 - my scan counts 29 bare heads on expressions.md where the card counted 26. The difference is exactly `Math` x1 and `new` x2 (JS built-ins, not scope roots), so the two readings reconcile. Architecture 4 and root README 7 reproduce exactly.",
    "FALSIFICATION 4 (dispatch text) - the dispatch's behaviour table is right at the VISIBILITY layer and wrong at the layer it names. `evaluateCondition` with no `data` key answers `true`; the raw `ExpressionEvaluator.evaluate` answers with the template's own SOURCE TEXT, not `true`. The `true` is the fail-soft verdict one layer up. Both measured, both stated in the migration note.",
    "NOT-YET-STALE (dispatch text) - the dispatch says the card's `data: dataSource` mechanism paragraph is now stale. On my base it is still LIVE: `packages/react/src/SchemaRenderer.tsx:847` still reads `data: dataSource`, because PR objectui#9369 is still open and draft (mergeable_state unstable, head 4de2534f2). It becomes stale when #9369 lands. The repair is correct in BOTH worlds: `PredicateScopeProvider` already exists and already feeds this evaluator on the base tree, and a conformant `DataSource` adapter never answered a `data.*` path anyway.",
    "SCOPE - the card's own addendum 5646840050 measured SIX more sites on content/docs/guide/schema-rendering.md (status x2, loading, items, error x2 at :231 :232 :479 :489 :504 :506) and concluded the surface count is four documents, not three. PR objectui#9369 does NOT move them (its hunks are at :68, :79-131, :409-446). The dispatch put that document out of scope, so the PR says `Part of #9297`, never a closing keyword, and names the half left open."
  ],
  "census_remeasured": {
    "base": "69aa9c017",
    "classifier": "SchemaRenderer elements matched with a word boundary after the name, so SchemaRendererProvider is excluded by construction - the card's own scan shape",
    "lit_control": "18 tag-shaped hits at base, reproducing the card's 18 exactly; 15 of them are real JSX elements once HTML comments are stripped. An empty offender list would therefore have been a reading.",
    "per_surface_base_to_head": {
      "content/docs/guide/expressions.md": {
        "tag_hits": "6 -> 3",
        "real_elements": "3 -> 3",
        "forwarded": "3 -> 0",
        "bare_heads": "29 (26 excluding Math/new) -> 26"
      },
      "content/docs/guide/architecture.md": {
        "tag_hits": "1 -> 1",
        "real_elements": "1 -> 1",
        "forwarded": "1 -> 0",
        "bare_heads": "4 -> 2"
      },
      "README.md": {
        "tag_hits": "2 -> 2",
        "real_elements": "2 -> 2",
        "forwarded": "2 -> 0",
        "bare_heads": "7 -> 7 (all kept, see judgements)"
      },
      "content/docs/guide/schema-rendering.md": {
        "note": "OUT OF SCOPE, untouched: 5 / 5 / 0 forwarded, 6 bare heads unchanged"
      },
      "packages/react/README.md": {
        "note": "OUT OF SCOPE, untouched: 4 / 4 / 0 forwarded, 0 bare heads"
      }
    },
    "forwarded_look_alikes_total": "6 at base across the three in-scope surfaces, 0 at head"
  },
  "per_site_judgement": {
    "rule_applied": "A head name MOVES to `record.` when the passage says the value is the row the surface is bound to. It STAYS BARE when the passage presents it as a value the host computed and published. After the objectui#9308 ruling the root set is OPEN - every key published through PredicateScopeProvider is a root - so the test is no longer 'is this name in the closed five-name set' but 'does the page publish this name and say so'.",
    "moved": [
      {
        "site": "expressions.md:148 disabledOn",
        "head": "form",
        "verdict": "moved to record.status - `form` is a root nothing in ObjectUI publishes at any tier"
      },
      {
        "site": "expressions.md:439 Dependent Fields",
        "head": "form",
        "verdict": "moved to record.country - a form's own values ARE the row under edit"
      },
      {
        "site": "expressions.md:470 Computed Fields",
        "head": "form",
        "verdict": "moved to record.price * record.quantity - same row"
      },
      {
        "site": "architecture.md:247 Conditional Rendering visible",
        "head": "form",
        "verdict": "moved to current_user.role - the ambient root the host's ExpressionProvider really publishes"
      },
      {
        "site": "architecture.md:248 Conditional Rendering disabled",
        "head": "form",
        "verdict": "moved to record.status"
      },
      {
        "site": "architecture.md:55 core topology row",
        "head": "data",
        "verdict": "moved to record.age - INVISIBLE to the census (data was in its accepted set) and the one site the ruling breaks"
      }
    ],
    "legitimate_left_bare": [
      {
        "site": "expressions.md x8",
        "head": "users",
        "why": "the page's running collection; a root the host publishes, now published and named in the Data Context section"
      },
      {
        "site": "expressions.md:172",
        "head": "settings",
        "why": "published in the same passage by the provider that block now mounts"
      },
      {
        "site": "expressions.md x2",
        "head": "price",
        "why": "host-computed value in Operators"
      },
      {
        "site": "expressions.md",
        "head": "score / count / total / items",
        "why": "same class - values the host computed and published"
      },
      {
        "site": "expressions.md x2",
        "head": "status",
        "why": "standalone nodes, not inside a record surface; moving them to record. would assert a row context the passage never establishes"
      },
      {
        "site": "expressions.md x2",
        "head": "task",
        "why": "a host-published object; same reasoning as status"
      },
      {
        "site": "expressions.md:567",
        "head": "formatCurrency",
        "why": "the card named this one - it sits in Custom Functions, where evaluateExpression is handed its OWN context. Legitimate by construction. Its surrounding prose still stated the retired scope and IS repaired."
      },
      {
        "site": "expressions.md:612",
        "head": "adultUsersScore",
        "why": "'pre-compute complex logic' - a pre-computed root the reader publishes; that IS the lesson"
      },
      {
        "site": "expressions.md:621 / :626",
        "head": "x / isAdmin",
        "why": "'use meaningful variable names' - a naming contrast; the names are root-level by construction and changing them destroys the lesson"
      },
      {
        "site": "architecture.md x2",
        "head": "orders",
        "why": "host-published collection in Data Transformations"
      },
      {
        "site": "README.md x7",
        "head": "stats",
        "why": "the flagship example's own bag - the bare name was always right; what was wrong is that it arrived as a forwarded prop. Now published through PredicateScopeProvider."
      },
      {
        "site": "expressions.md",
        "head": "item / index",
        "why": "excluded up front by the card - list renderers publish them through a different mechanism. Untouched."
      },
      {
        "site": "expressions.md",
        "head": "Math / new",
        "why": "JS built-ins, not scope roots - the 29-vs-26 difference"
      }
    ],
    "totals": "37 bare head names in the card's population: 5 moved, 32 judged legitimate. Plus 1 `data.*` site the census could not see, also moved. No find-and-replace was run."
  },
  "both_halves_moved_together": "Confirmed per site. Every one of the six forwarded look-alikes became the provider that actually carries the value (PredicateScopeProvider for the expression scope, SchemaRendererProvider for the adapter and for debug), and in the SAME commit every head name on that page was judged against the scope the tree builds and the page states, page-wide, where names come from. No surface got its wiring moved while its prefixes were left unjudged - which is exactly objectui#8021 leg D.",
  "debug_mode_block": "Both wrong props fixed together, not one. `expressions.md` Debug Mode wrote data={...} AND debug={true} on the element; debug is read off the provider context (context?.debug || context?.debugFlags?.enabled), so both were forwarded and neither did anything. The block is now a SchemaRendererProvider mount with dataSource={null} (that prop is required by the provider's declared type and this mount is about the flag), and the prose names the mechanism for both props. NOTE: that fence is a DECLARED FRAGMENT, so check:doc-snippets parses but does not compile it - the API was verified by reading packages/react/src/context/SchemaRendererContext.tsx, not by the gate.",
  "migration_note_states_the_flip": "Yes, and it does not merely rename a provider. The note in expressions.md states: a missing root and a present-but-undefined root are not the same; `visible: \"${data.x}\"` used to resolve to undefined and HIDE its node on every row, and with no `data` key it is unevaluable, the surface fails soft, and the node is SHOWN; the runtime-layer row root is `record` (ADR-0089 D3), so such a gate is rewritten to record.* rather than re-publishing a `data` key. architecture.md carries the short form of the same statement.",
  "summary": "Repaired the three teaching surfaces objectui#9297 scoped. All six forwarded look-alikes (expressions.md x3 including the Debug Mode block's two props, architecture.md x1, root README x2) became the provider that actually carries the value, matching PR objectui#9369's shape: PredicateScopeProvider for the expression scope, SchemaRendererProvider for the adapter and for debug, and each page now states that dataSource is the adapter and not a root. All 37 bare head names were judged individually - 5 moved to record.*, 32 judged legitimate under the open root set the ruling creates. One extra site the census was structurally blind to (architecture.md:55 `${data.age > 18}`) was found and moved. The expressions.md Expression Errors claim, which the card's addendum left NOT MEASURED, was measured, found false in both directions, and repaired in place because the same PR now states the opposite two sections above it.",
  "tests": "All at head 20831dc1d; heavy runs serialised through ../objectstack/scripts/pm/os-verify-lock.sh with a stable slot (OS_VERIFY_LOCK_SLOT=issue-9297). VERDICT lines, verbatim: (1) 'os-verify-lock: VERDICT command-exit 1 - held the lock 21s - waited 162s (2m42s)' for the build + first doc-snippets run [build 'Tasks: 35 successful, 35 total', BUILD EXIT=0; doc-snippets 'Semantic phase: 650 of 650 block(s) judged, 3 failed.' EXIT=1, all three inherited]; (2) 'os-verify-lock: VERDICT command-exit 0 - held the lock 24s - waited 35s' for the named-witness run [Test Files 6 passed (6), Tests 112 passed (112)]; (3) 'os-verify-lock: VERDICT command-exit 0 - held the lock 25s - waited 0s' for the final run at 20831dc1d [witnesses 6/6, 112/112; doc-snippets 650/650 judged 3 failed - the same three inherited; doc-fences EXIT=0]. check:doc-snippets' own controls all fired (resolution resolved @object-ui/types to the built dist/index.d.ts, sentinel produced TS2305, positive produced 0), so the reading is a reading and not a degraded harness. Unlocked gates, exit code captured before any pipe: check:doc-fences EXIT=0, check-doc-component-types EXIT=0, check-doc-example-ids EXIT=0, check-doc-links EXIT=0, check-control-bytes EXIT=0, check-changeset-presence EXIT=0, check-changeset-claims EXIT=0 (report-only), check-doc-expression-carriage EXIT=0 (report-only), check-governed-queue-guard --test on the three paths: 'NOT GOVERNED - 3 path(s) checked against 5 governed surface(s); none matched'. Gate family derived BY HAND from package.json + .github/workflows (no dispatch-gates.mjs in this repo). Named witnesses derived by hand from scripts/markdown-test-inputs.mjs, not guessed: page-body-single-node-8310.test.tsx reads the root README (it pins the Basic Usage schema literal's `children` spelling, `type: \"grid\"`, three `type: \"statistic\"` and the three labels - my edits touch only the wiring around that literal, not the literal) plus four tests walking content/docs/**; the objectui#8021 pin was run too even though its TEACHING_SURFACES are the two out-of-scope documents. Behaviour measurements on the BUILT evaluator (packages/core/dist), each with a firing control: evaluateCondition with {data: undefined} => false, with no data key => true, control {record:{status:'draft'}} => true vs {record:{status:'open'}} => false; ${user.invalidProperty} with user published => undefined, with no user root => the source text \"${user.invalidProperty}\", control ${user.name} => \"Alice\"; ${stats.users} with stats published => 1234, with nothing published => the source text. No ablation was needed or run - this PR adds no guard.",
  "mcp_calls": "0 - every GitHub read and write went through repo-scoped REST (probe: GET /repos/objectstack-ai/objectui HTTP 200) plus git; the card, its three comments, objectui#9308's five comments, PR #9369's metadata and its diff (fetched into refs/i9297/pr9369), the PR create and the PR patch. Channel declared: REST. MCP search_issues was not used and no duplicate-search was needed - nothing was filed.",
  "inherited_reds": [
    "Doc Snippet Type Check - the three doc-snippet failures are content/docs/guide/schema-rendering.md:99, :434 and packages/react/README.md:73, all TS2740, all on the two surfaces this card forbids touching. They are objectui#9346 verbatim and PR objectui#9369 is what moves them. Not repaired here.",
    "Bundle Analysis - arrived on main with objectui#9316, a maintainer decision. Not repaired here."
  ],
  "changeset": "Not owed, by measurement: `node scripts/check-changeset-presence.mjs` - '3 file(s) changed, 0 of them published source of a package the release covers, 0 of them a manifest whose published contract moved, 0 under a package changesets ignores, 0 changeset(s) added. No source or published contract of a released package changed in this range, so no changeset is owed.' No empty-frontmatter changeset written and, per the dispatch, no skip-changeset label applied in this repo.",
  "governed_surface": "NOT GOVERNED - the three paths were tested against scripts/check-governed-queue-guard.mjs GOVERNED_SURFACES and none matched. The PR is an ordinary one. I did not flip ready, arm auto-merge, enqueue, or apply any label. Clause-2 stayed `no`: no packages/*/README.md that check:readme-exports grades and no source file was touched.",
  "open_questions": [
    {
      "question": "Does this PR close objectui#9297, or does the card's own addendum keep it open? The addendum (5646840050) raises the surface count to FOUR documents by adding six sites on content/docs/guide/schema-rendering.md, which the dispatch put out of scope and which PR objectui#9369 does not move either.",
      "options": [
        "A - leave the PR as `Part of #9297` (what I did): the card stays open carrying the six schema-rendering.md sites, and someone dispatches them once #9369 lands.",
        "B - use a closing keyword against this card in the PR body and file the six sites as a follow-up card at merge time.",
        "C - use a closing keyword and accept losing them (rejected: merging would silently close the card and the six sites would disappear from every open-issue sweep)."
      ],
      "recommendation": "A, because it is the only option that is safe under the merge-time closing-keyword parser and needs no second actor before this PR lands. B is fine too if the PM prefers a clean card boundary, but it requires the follow-up card to exist BEFORE the merge, and #9369 has to land first for the six sites' line numbers to be stable."
    },
    {
      "question": "The PR body PATCH appended a second, bare attribution footer (+58 bytes, exactly AGENTS.md mutation 3). The session-URL footer and the prose session mention both survived. Per AGENTS.md I did not loop re-posting. Flagging it so the PM does not read the duplicate as sloppiness."
    }
  ],
  "out_of_scope_findings": [
    "noted, not filed: AGENTS.md section 3 quotes the same retired spelling this PR repairs at architecture.md:55 - the @object-ui/core topology row writes the expression engine's example as a data.age gate. Not touched: AGENTS.md is a governed surface and one path there would move this whole PR to the human-merge route. Carrier: whoever next edits that table - there is no other PR or person queued on it today.",
    "noted, not filed: content/docs/guide/expressions.md :226 / :242 author ${users} on `list.items`, a key with no carriage row. Pre-existing, unchanged by this PR, and reported (report-only) by check-doc-expression-carriage, whose own header routes this class to objectui#7440 / #7444 / #7838. Carrier: those three cards.",
    "noted, not filed: the card's own addendum already carries the six remaining sites on content/docs/guide/schema-rendering.md - it is not a new finding, it is the scope question in open_questions. Carrier: objectui#9297 itself.",
    "repaired in place, not filed: content/docs/guide/expressions.md Expression Errors stated a throw that does not happen. Measured (see tests), found wrong in both directions, repaired in the second commit under the bounded carve-out - same defect class, mechanical, no other claim on this file, same gate family, no new verification surface. Declared here rather than left silent."
  ]
}


